publican, though one rates it Lean R and prediction markets give Flood about an 82% chance. A September poll from a Democratic firm showed the race essentially tied, and the two debated in late September over Iran, prices, and experience. The forecast expects Flood to win by a moderate margin, with the race competitive enough to watch but tilting Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1466, "margin": -6.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1237, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1206, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2177, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1689, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1777, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2315, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1394, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1156, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}]}